<title>EGYPT: British Gas makes first find in Rosetta concession.</title>
<headline>British Gas makes first find in Rosetta concession.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Gas Plc has made its first discovery of gas in its Rosetta concession off the northern coast of Egypt, state television said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A discovery well yielded 20 million cubic feet of gas a day at test on a first layer 1,100 metres deep. Tests on two deeper layers are under way, it added.</p>
<p>The discovery is 50 km (30 miles) northeast of Rosetta town and 70 km (40 miles) northeast of the Abu Qir field.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
